# ── Docs: ignore working notes, keep the documentation ───────────────────────
# The blanket rule below is deliberate: dated audits, runbooks and session
# notes do not belong in the repo. It was too blanket, and that cost months.
#
# docs/ is documentation people are meant to read ON GITHUB. The *.md rule
# swallowed it, so the guides split out of the README were never committed,
# their links 404'd for everyone who clicked them, and a commit went in on the
# remote removing the LINKS rather than adding the FILES. One line here caused
# all of it, and nothing reported it because an ignored file is not an error.
*.md
# Root README only -- an anchored pattern, so a stray nested markdown cannot
# slip back in through the negation.
!/README.md
# Documentation that is meant to be read, and the two model cards, one of which
# a test reads off disk.
!/docs/*.md
!/STATUS.md
!/HF_MODEL_CARD.md
# The native build guide, linked from the root README.
!/native/README.md

# Run artefacts from the corpus tools. Reports of a measurement, not source,
# and pilot_clipping.json has already been committed once by accident.
/pilot_clipping.json
/survey.json

# Audit, review and status reports stay local too. These were written as HTML so
# they slipped past the *.md rule and stayed tracked; the same content belongs in
# the code's own docstrings, not in dated files that go stale in the repo.
AUDIT_*.html
*_REVIEW_*.html
COMPETITIVE_*.html
*_AUDIT_*.html

# Master EXRs written by RUDRA Studio -- deliverables, not source.
ui/_masters/

# The one committed checkpoint (see checkpoints/README.md). Weights are
# otherwise never committed -- *.pth above, and everything under the data dir.
!checkpoints/
!checkpoints/*.pt
!checkpoints/README.md
# Shipped weights are the *.pt at the checkpoints root. A training run
# writes a subdirectory (best.pt, step_*.pt, train.jsonl); those are
# run outputs, not releases -- promote one by copying it up a level.
checkpoints/*/
# Exported bench trees (ref/test/baseline/sdr PNGs): gigabytes, regenerable.
/bench/

# secrets -- nothing matched a scan on 3 Sep 2026; this keeps it that way
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
**/credentials*

# Third-party method clones for the §9 comparison. Cloned beside the repo by
# training/run_expandnet.py and friends; not ours to vendor, and each carries
# its own .git, so staging one commits a gitlink with no .gitmodules and hands
# everyone who clones RUDRA an empty directory.
hdr-expandnet/
Deep-HdrReconstruction/
hdrcnn/
SingleHDR/

# The v1 draft is superseded by paper/main.pdf (mirrored as
# research/RUDRA_HDR_2026.pdf). Kept locally, out of the published repo.
research/RUDRA_V01.pdf

# Scratch and session notes. NEXT_*.md is already covered by the *.md rule
# above; COMMITMSG.txt is not, and it kept getting committed by hand.
scratch/
COMMITMSG.txt
NEXT_*.md
AGENTS.md
.agents/

# Local helper scripts: they carry absolute paths from this machine and are
# regenerated per task. Not part of the project.
COMMIT_*.ps1
/AUDIT_*.ps1
SCRUB_TRAILERS.txt

# Repo housekeeping (22 Sep 2026): one-shot scripts and dated reports
# live out of the root and out of git.
/scripts/archive/
/scripts/finalize_*.ps1
/scripts/next_*.ps1
/scripts/critical_*.ps1
/scripts/RUN_CRITICAL_PATH.bat
/scripts/RUN_NEXT_STEPS.bat
/reports/
